64625729050375,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":29.6,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.009255910421173158,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":30.2,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.05131008057694258,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":51.3,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.030893974551639145,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":45.4,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.004337003487608961,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":92.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.0066799996,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":4.5,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"NorthWestern Energy Group, Inc., doing business as NorthWestern Energy, provides electricity and natural gas to residential, commercial, and diversified industrial customers. It generates, purchases, transmits, and distributes electricity; and produces, purchases, stores, transmits, and distributes natural gas, as well as owns municipal franchises to provide natural gas service in the communities. The company operates 6,596 miles of electric transmission and 18,946 miles of electric distribution lines with approximately 397 transmission and distribution substations; and 2,133 miles of natural gas transmission and 5,939 miles of natural gas distribution lines with approximately 134 city gate stations in Montana. It also operates 1,344 miles of electric transmission and 2,386 miles of electric distribution lines in South Dakota with approximately 123 transmission and distribution substations; and 55 miles of natural gas transmission, 1,853 miles of natural gas distribution lines in South Dakota, and 836 miles of natural gas distribution lines Nebraska. The company provides electricity and/or natural gas to approximately 850,300 customers in Montana, South Dakota, Nebraska, and Yellowstone National Park. NorthWestern Energy Group, Inc. was incorporated in 1923 and is based in Sioux Falls, South Dakota.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Brian B. Bird | CEO, President & Director | Age 65 | Compensation: $2.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $966K ranks in the below the sector median among Utilities peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["NorthWestern Energy Group, Inc. is a mid-cap utilities business with a $5.2B market cap on $1.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $130M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 100% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.998290532436084},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 60/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Regulatory rate-case risk and rising cost of capital \u2014 the allowed return is set by commissions, and the business lives or dies by that negotiation.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Grid modernisation capex burden \u2014 aging infrastructure requires massive reinvestment that regulators may not fully allow into rate base, compressing earned returns.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","18 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How Investors Are Reacting To NorthWestern Energy Group (NWE) Mixed Q3 Earnings","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/utilities/nasdaq-nwe/northwestern-energy-group/news/how-investors-are-reacting-to-northwestern-energy-group-nwe-1","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794572801.251,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.103,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"(NWE) Movement as an Input in Quant Signal Sets","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","li